  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Budapest University of Economics and Business (BUEB) is Hungary’s largest business-focused higher education institution. Established in 1857 as the Pest Academy of Commerce, it stands as the second-oldest business school globally.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At BUEB, you’ll be part of a vibrant student life. The university organises a variety of events, including cultural festivals, conferences, and workshops, so you can make professional contacts as well.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>BUEB provides several accommodation options to ensure you have a comfortable living experience. The residences are located in the heart of Budapest and offer modern facilities. The university also collaborates with various private housing providers to offer a range of shared apartments and private rooms.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The BUEB Library Network, established in 2000, supports all your academic needs. It includes three faculty libraries and a Tourism Library, offering you access to a wide range of e-books, journals, and databases to help you with research and studies.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>At the university, you can play various sports activities, including basketball, volleyball, football, and tennis. You can also participate in competitive sports events through leagues and tournaments.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
